{"Version":2,"ProgramText":"; \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n;  BOING!\n;\n;  The Amiga\u0027s own demo from 1984: a red and white ball that turns\n;  as it bounces in front of a purple grid, its shadow on the wall\n;  behind it. Here to a ProTracker module, the music the Amiga\n;  played on its four sample channels (Sound/Tracker/MODs).\n;\n;  Layer 0: the wall and the floor   Layer 1: the shadow and the ball\n;  Layer 2: the scroller at the top, a rainbow on the red of its font\n; \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSCREEN 640,480\nMUSIC PLAY \u0022Sound/Tracker/MODs/Introgasm.MOD\u0022\n\n; \u2500\u2500 Layer 0: the grey wall with its purple grid, and the floor in perspective \u2500\u2500\nSCREEN SELECT 0\nINKG \u0022#A8A8A8\u0022\nBAR 0, 0, 639, 479\nINKG \u0022#A000A0\u0022\nFOR X = 40 TO 600 STEP 40\n  LINE X, 40, X, 360\nNEXT X\nFOR Y = 40 TO 360 STEP 40\n  LINE 40, Y, 600, Y\nNEXT Y\nFOR X = 40 TO 600 STEP 40\n  LINE X, 360, 320 + (X - 320) * 1.5, 479\nNEXT X\nFOR K = 1 TO 4\n  Y = INT(360 + K * K * 7.4)\n  W = INT(280 * (1 + (Y - 360) / 119 * 0.5))\n  LINE 320 - W, Y, 320 + W, Y\nNEXT K\n\n; \u2500\u2500 Layer 1: the ball, 15 pictures of a turn, and its shadow: the same ball, dark and see-through \u2500\u2500\nSPRITE LOAD 1, \u0022Graphics/Anim/Anim_AmigaBall_B15.png\u0022, 92, 92, 15\nSPRITE LOAD 2, \u0022Graphics/Anim/Anim_AmigaBall_B15.png\u0022, 92, 92, 15\nFOR I = 1 TO 2\n  SPRITE HANDLE I, 46, 46\n  SPRITE ZOOM I, 180\n  SPRITE LAYER I, 1\n  SPRITE ON I\nNEXT I\nSPRITE EFFECT ADD 1, COLOR, 0.15, 1, 0\nSPRITE ALPHA 1, 120\n\n; \u2500\u2500 Layer 2: the scroller \u2500\u2500\nSCREEN SELECT 2\nFONT LOAD 0, \u0022Graphics/font.png\u0022, 32, 25\nFONT MAP 0, \u0022ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ!?:;0123456789@()\u00A3$%.\u2019[]\u201D,-\u0022\nRASTER 1, 0, 0, 40, \u0022Yellow, Orange, Red, Magenta, Cyan, Yellow\u0022\nRASTER WRAP 1, TRUE\nRASTER COLOUR 2, \u0022Red\u0022\nTXT$ = \u0022                    BOING!   THE AMIGA DEMO FROM 1984, REMADE IN AMOS LIKE BASIC.\u0022\nTXT$ = TXT$ & \u0022   A BALL SHEET OF 15 PICTURES, A SHADOW WITH SPRITE EFFECT COLOR AND SPRITE ALPHA,\u0022\nTXT$ = TXT$ & \u0022 AND A PROTRACKER MODULE ON FOUR CHANNELS, AS PAULA PLAYED IT...   \u0022\nCW = 32\nSX = 0 : T = 0\nX = 160 : DX = 2.6 : F = 0\n\n; \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nLoop:\n  T = T + 1\n\n  ; Across the screen and back, and up and down as a bouncing ball does\n  X = X + DX\n  IF X > 500 OR X < 140 THEN DX = -DX\n  Y = 310 - ABS(SIN(T * 2.1)) * 180\n  ; It turns the way it goes: forwards to the right, backwards to the left\n  IF DX > 0 THEN F = F + 1 ELSE F = F + 14\n  F = F MOD 15\n  SPRITE FRAME 1, F : SPRITE FRAME 2, F\n  SPRITE POS 2, X, Y\n  SPRITE POS 1, X + 44, Y + 18\n\n  ; The scroller\n  SX = SX + 3\n  IF SX >= LEN(TXT$) * CW THEN SX = 0\n  FONT CLEAR\n  FONT PRINT #2, 0, -(SX MOD CW), 8, MID$(TXT$ & TXT$, INT(SX / CW) + 1, 21)\n  RASTER #2, MOVE 1, (T * 2) MOD 40\n\n  WAIT VBL\nGOTO Loop\n","ScreenWidth":null,"ScreenHeight":null,"Sprites":null,"MapWidth":null,"MapHeight":null,"MapData":null}